  "title": "U.S. suspends Microsoft, Adobe, and major IT firms from green card program",
  "summary": "The U.S. Labor Department has suspended Cognizant, Infosys, Tata, Wipro, HCL, Capgemini, and Microsoft from the permanent labor certification program, citing multiple active federal investigations related to their participation in the program.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. Labor Department suspended Cognizant, Infosys, Tata, Wipro, HCL, Capgemini, and Microsoft from the permanent labor certification program.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Labor Secretary Keith Sonderling cited multiple active federal investigations around the companies' involvement in the program.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The suspension includes major IT firms and companies related to the U.S. green card program.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
